4:[["$","$Le",null,{}],["$","main",null,{"className":"container","children":["$","article",null,{"className":"page-module__hUlLAq__article","children":[["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/#blog","className":"page-module__hUlLAq__back","children":"← Back to blog"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-module__hUlLAq__meta","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Engineering"}],["$","time",null,{"dateTime":"2026-07-28","children":["2026-07-28"," · ","5 min read"]}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"Clean API Integration Patterns"}],["$","img",null,{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=85","alt":"","className":"page-module__hUlLAq__image"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"page-module__hUlLAq__excerpt","children":"How thoughtful request boundaries and predictable error handling make full stack features easier to ship."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-module__hUlLAq__content","children":[["$","p","API integrations become easier to maintain when the UI does not need to know every detail about the underlying service. A small data-access layer can normalize responses and keep components focused on presentation.",{"children":"API integrations become easier to maintain when the UI does not need to know every detail about the underlying service. A small data-access layer can normalize responses and keep components focused on presentation."}],["$","p","Every request should have a clear loading, success, and failure state. These states are part of the product experience, not an afterthought added once the happy path works.",{"children":"Every request should have a clear loading, success, and failure state. These states are part of the product experience, not an afterthought added once the happy path works."}],["$","p","Typed contracts, consistent naming, and useful logs help teams debug issues quickly while keeping future integrations predictable.",{"children":"Typed contracts, consistent naming, and useful logs help teams debug i